    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25PFxuq2GjykReQ26LTWPmi)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Order: independent of the `sp-fetch-inbox` hints PR, but both need the same helper. The `sp-fetch-inbox` hints PR did not exist when I started, so this PR adds the helper as the new module `sp-echo-hints` (`sp-echo-hints-mode`, `sp-echo-hints-format`, `sp-echo-hints-show`).\n- If the other PR already has a helper: merge that one first, then reduce this module to it (keep one of the two; the `(KEY . LABEL)` list format is the thing to match).\n- If merged first: nothing breaks; the `sp-fetch-inbox` PR then reuses `sp-echo-hints` instead of its own.\n- Conflicts with: `README.org` module table and `init.el` module list (one added line each); keep both lines.\n- After merging: restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`); nothing to retarget.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Request:** the key lists in the header lines of the linting and batch interfaces do not wrap; show them in the echo area like `nano-help.el` of nano-emacs.\n- **New module `sp-echo-hints`** (doc `docs/tangles/funct/sp-echo-hints.org`):\n  - `sp-echo-hints-mode` shows a buffer's hints when Emacs is idle and the echo area is empty, so a command's own message is never replaced.\n  - A hint is `(KEY . LABEL)`; the key is bold. Hints that do not fit the frame width are dropped from the end and marked with \"…\".\n  - Not written to `*Messages*`.\n  - Options: `sp-echo-hints-delay`, `sp-echo-hints-separator`, face `sp-echo-hints-key`.\n- **Converted:**\n  - `sp-batch-report-mode`: used by every batch command (litnote titles/refs/meta, author notes, tag lint, normalise, BibTeX lint, property conversion).\n  - Footnote lint: keys moved to the echo area; the header line keeps only the scan/apply progress. The obsolete old report mode follows too.\n  - Litnote status table: counts stay in the header line; its keys are now hints.\n- **Left as they were** (keys are text inside the buffer, not a header): author-notes report, tag-lint report footer, backlink check, graph view. Say if you want them converted too.\n- Docs are bullet lists; `when-let*` only; no CHANGELOG edit.\n- **Tested** (Emacs 29.3 batch): 8 new ERT tests for `sp-echo-hints`; the 17 `sp-batch-report` tests pass; syntax check of all touched modules; the `.el` files are re-tangled from the docs.\n- **Untested by Claude:** the footnote lint and litnote status table (their test files need the real `sp-globals` environment), the GUI and idle timing on macOS, and how it looks with your theme and echo-area font.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 457-echo-area-hints-linting; git checkout 457-echo-area-hints-linting`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/funct -l tests/sp-echo-hints-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` → 8 pass\n- [ ] `M-x sp-litnotes-titles-dryrun` (or any dry run): the header line no longer lists keys; after about half a second the echo area shows `RET visit   n/p link   d drop ...` with bold keys (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] In that report press `n`: a command message (for example after `d`: the drop message) stays; the hints return once it clears\n- [ ] Narrow the frame: the last hints are replaced by \"…\" instead of wrapping\n- [ ] `M-x sp-org-lint-footnotes-dryrun`: header shows the progress while scanning; the keys appear in the echo area when it is ready (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-status-report`: header counts unchanged; hints show `m/u mark/unmark ...` (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Open the minibuffer (`M-x`) in a report: hints do not overwrite the prompt\n- [ ] Regression: `RET`, `d`, `u`, `A`, `g`, `q` in a report still work; `*Messages*` has no hint lines\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard any local edits made while testing: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (and `git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Return to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 457-echo-area-hints-linting`; the remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed.\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) so the config matches main again.\n- These commands do not change the vault; the dry runs only read it.\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiA3876SADjpTLYKDZ5)_",
